 "drug_rule": "Alpha-1 antagonists are contraindicated in patients with neurogenic bladder because they can impair the ability to achieve and maintain an adequate bladder contraction. In neurogenic bladder, the primary goal is to facilitate smooth muscle contraction, not to relax the bladder neck or urethra. Additionally, alpha-1 antagonists are associated with a dose-dependent increase in orthostatic hypotension, which is particularly dangerous in adolescents due to the ongoing development of the autonomic nervous system.",
