 "drug_rule": "Fenofibrate is primarily hepatically metabolized, but its active metabolite fenocaprate is renally eliminated. In mild renal impairment, fenocaprate accumulation can cause hepatotoxicity, myopathy, and rhabdomyolysis. The combination of fenofibrate and atorvastatin is contraindicated in mild renal impairment due to the risk of additive myopathy and rhabdomyolysis. Additionally, the high atorvastatin dose (40 mg) is already at the upper limit for many patients; adding fenofibrate without dose adjustment or monitoring increases the risk of statin-induced myopathy.",
