 "drug_rule": "Loperamide is a substrate of CYP3A4 and can cause constipation, which may alter the transit time of HIV/HCV medications. Ritonavir is a potent CYP3A4 inhibitor, so reduced clearance of ritonavir could elevate its plasma concentration, increasing the risk of QT prolongation, hepatotoxicity, or other adverse effects. Loperamide is also a central nervous system depressant and can worsen respiratory depression in patients with underlying respiratory impairment, though no baseline respiratory impairment is documented.\n\n3.",
